1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Vesper v0.2 adds a second proof: Ed25519 on Solana.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,200
Light a vigil the same way. Nothing leaves the browser.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:12,300
One minute, kept against the wall clock.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:15,000
When it is kept, the return offers a Solana seal.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Forge a keeper here. A passphrase wraps it; the key lives only in memory.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,300
It locks. It opens for this visit only, and locks again after fifteen quiet minutes.

7
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:26,000
Unlocked, it signs one canonical message: cluster, sigil, times, outcome, clock evidence, seal.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,300
The app checks the signature and the seal before it keeps anything.

9
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,200
Nothing is sent to the cluster. The record verifies offline, and the crypt names its chain.

10
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:38,600
A command-line verifier checks the same record without trusting the app.
